=== {{S|étymologie}} ===
: {{composé de|m=1|lang=en|actual|-ly}}.

=== {{S|adverbe|en}} ===
'''actually''' {{pron|ˈæk.tʃu.ə.li|en}}
# [[en fait|En fait]].
#* {{exemple | lang=en | Our atmosphere appears blue, but '''actually''' it’s due to the refraction of the sunlight hitting the atmosphere.}}
#* {{exemple | lang=en
 | Suppose the world was '''actually''' governed by classical mechanics.
 | source=lien=https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/physics/8-04-quantum-physics-i-spring-2013/assignments/MIT8_04S13_ps1.pdf|Allan Adams, ''8:04 Quantum Mechanics — Problem Set 1'', [[w:Massachusetts Institute of Technology|Massachusetts Institute of Technology]], 05/02/2013}}
# [[en réalité|En réalité]], [[en vérité]], [[vraiment]].
#* {{exemple | lang=en
 | He was the first and certainly not the last to point out that BIOS '''actually''' stands for “Basic Input/Output System,” not “Built-In Operating System” as I have it here (and as it ''ought'' to be); but I feel that I am entitled to trample all other considerations into the dirt in my pursuit of a satisfying pun, so this part of the book is unchanged.
 | source={{w|Neal {{pc|Stephenson}}}}, ''{{w|Le Samouraï virtuel|Snow Crash}}'', 1992 (éd. 1993), {{ISBN|0-553-08853-X}}}}

